SUMMARY:Wye Junction Park Grand Opening Block Party
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the opening of Wye Junction Park\, a new outdoor gathering space and gateway to the future Durham Rail Trail in downtown Durham’s Warehouse District. Free and open to the public\, the community event will feature: \nMusic + Movement\nLive outdoor music from 8-Track Minds\nA free mat Pilates class led by soon-to-open retailer Pilates Addiction from 5-5:30 p.m. (Reserve your spot here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1989235303341?aff=oddtdtcreator)\nBull City Run Club with Bull City Running Co. starting at 6 p.m. \nArt + Experiences\nThe unveiling of a 35-foot public art mural by Durham artist BC Crabtree\nAn “Ask Me Anything” experience with BC Crabtree\nInteractive art experiences\, including the creation of a collaborative art piece with local artist Jane Cheek \nFood + Drink\nFood and drinks from neighboring retailers like Timber Pizza Co.\, The Blue Note Grill\, Durham Distillery & More\nLocal food trucks throughout the evening\, including MexiArepa Grill and Baton Rouge Cuisine \nExplore Wye Junction\nA site history booth with Preservation Durham\nOptional tours of the Wye Junction community
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/wye-junction-park-grand-opening-block-party/
LOCATION:Wye Junction Park\, 701 Washington St.\, Durham\, 27701
CATEGORIES:Art,Author / Artist Visit,Classes & Workshops,Community Engagement,Concert,Cultural,Festival,Fitness,Food & Drink,Food Vendors/Food Trucks,Free,History,Kid Friendly,Live Performance,Music,Outdoors
